%I A220879 #27 Aug 27 2026 13:11:29
%S A220879 0,1,0,0,7,7281,468822749,1392052397151934248
%N A220879 Number of inequivalent monotone Boolean functions of n variables with no symmetries.
%H A220879 Bartłomiej Pawelski, <a href="https://bip.ug.edu.pl/st-tyt_nauk/117481/bartlomiej_pawelski">Counting and generating monotone Boolean functions</a>, Doctoral Diss., Univ. Gdańsk, (Poland, 2024). See pp. 46, 49.
%H A220879 Bartlomiej Pawelski and Andrzej Szepietowski, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2302.04615">Divisibility properties of Dedekind numbers</a>, arXiv:2302.04615 [math.CO], 2023. See Table 6 p. 15.
%H A220879 Tamon Stephen and Timothy Yusun, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/1209.4623">Counting inequivalent monotone Boolean functions</a>, arXiv preprint arXiv:1209.4623 [cs.DS], 2012.
%F A220879 a(n) = (1/n!)*Sum_{H <= S_n} mu(1,H)*F(H) = Sum_{[H] <= S_n} mu(1,H)*F(H)/|N_{S_n}(H)|, where F(H) is the number of monotone Boolean functions on n variables invariant under every permutation in H, the second sum is over conjugacy classes of subgroups H of S_n, mu is the Möbius function of the subgroup lattice of S_n, and N_{S_n}(H) is the normalizer of H in S_n. - _Vladeta Jovovic_, Aug 27 2026
%Y A220879 Cf. A003182.
%K A220879 nonn,more,changed
%O A220879 1,5
%A A220879 _N. J. A. Sloane_, Dec 28 2012
